title: Foundation::_sync_pull aborts the whole run when one repo's pull refuses
updated: 2026-08-13T02:22:26Z
---

Found by the ref-worker while fixing #154, in a file outside its lane.

Foundation.pm:497 (_sync_pull) calls $git->pull unguarded, and its caller
at :439 has no eval. So a pull that refuses aborts the ENTIRE
karr-foundation run rather than skipping the one repo and moving on.

Pre-existing: the wholesale-wipe guard and the board-identity guard
already die there. But #154 adds a third trigger, and the stale-lock case
will be the common one -- a .lock left behind by a killed karr on one
board now takes down every other board's tick with it.

The drain loop already isolates per repo one level down: _process_repo is
wrapped in a try that warns and moves on (Foundation.pm:286), and
_drain_repo likewise (:451). The pull sits just outside that protection.

Fix direction: bring the pull inside the same per-repo isolation, so a
refusal warns, marks that board's outcome as an error, releases whatever
it holds, and lets the run continue. Take care that a board which cannot
pull is NOT then processed as if it were up to date -- skipping it is the
point.
